--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Presidio — MIT
Copyright (c) Presidio Contributors
https://github.com/data-privacy-stack/presidio

Regex patterns, context word lists, score constants, entity type names and test
expectations are derived from Presidio. MIT permits this; attribution is to
"Presidio Contributors" rather than Microsoft, following the project's own
LICENSE after its move to the data-privacy-stack organisation.

  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/recognizers.json
  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/recognizer_data.json
  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/iban_countries.json
  Tests/PresidioConformance/Fixtures/*.json

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Public Suffix List — Mozilla Public License 2.0
https://publicsuffix.org/

Used by the email recognizer to identify registrable domains. MPL-2.0 is
file-level copyleft, so the list is kept in its own file with the upstream
notice preserved rather than merged into the MIT-licensed data around it. IDN
suffixes are punycoded at extraction time; the transformation is in
Tools/extract_recognizer_data.py.

  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/public_suffix_list.json

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
libphonenumber — Apache License 2.0
Copyright (C) 2009 The Libphonenumber Authors
https://github.com/google/libphonenumber

Phone number metadata and the matcher's own regular expressions, obtained via
the python-phonenumbers port (also Apache-2.0). The parsing, validation and
matching algorithms in Sources/PresidioRecognizers/PhoneNumber*.swift are ported
from that implementation.

  Sources/PresidioRecognizers/Resources/phone_metadata.json

